  "scopeLimits": [
    "Only POST /users/memberships and its inline ten-field decoder changed. DELETE, other handlers, schemas, shared helpers, policies and migrations are unchanged.",
    "Administrators by legacy flag and global binding enroll through real HTTP/TOTP in the same session family. No positive MFA proof is fabricated by SQL.",
    "Baseline has sixteen201 versus403 failures. Twelve verify complete persisted membership DTO, audit, windows and eligibility on the target user original HTTP token; four verify the same effects with narrow proof-removing triggers.",
    "Four narrow AFTER INSERT/UPDATE membership or AFTER INSERT audit trigger cases cover creation and readmission. Each fires once, with exact restoration of memberships, audits and original proof timestamp text/generation/presence after fixed rollback.",
    "Positive cases preserve ten-field public DTO, IDs, createdAt, future/current windows, inactive/expired readmission and eligibility changes on the same HTTP token. Local managers are optional-MFA, constrained to their building; residents cannot admit users.",
    "Recent password verification is required for BUILDING_ADMIN grants and recovers via real HTTP verification. Routine RESIDENT admission, schema validation and foreign-key refusals retain their contracts.",
    "V1 was stopped at a TypeScript assertion-narrowing error; no functional V1 run occurred. V2 adds only the Row generic annotation, with identical runtime assertions, cases and product.",
    "All preparations, types and functional runs used the unchanged1536MiB guard. User authorized pausing two other-project containers, but both were observed already exited and this task did not stop them or restart the computer.",
    "Fifteen regression files retain their own limits. Historical runs and baseline are not added to corrected counts.",
    "DELETE self-revocation, support/features commands, other domains, cache policy, generic trigger exceptions, promotion and actual PostgreSQL lock waits remain outside this acceptance.",
    "No browser, native Android/iOS, full API, performance, universal commit-boundary guarantee or production acceptance is asserted."
  ],
